{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>A prophet from among you, from your brothers, like me</b>. The reason for <b>מִקִּרְבְּךָ</b> (\"from among you\") is to hint that prophecy exists only in the land of Israel, and therefore Scripture says of it (Isaiah 22:1), \"The burden of the valley of vision,\" just as our Rabbis mentioned (Mekhilta, beginning of Bo). And likewise the reason for <b>מֵאַחֶיךָ</b> (\"from your brothers\") is that HaShem has given you superiority over all the nations, and He will not place His spirit except upon you — like me, for from among your brothers He will establish one for you in my stead, and so on from prophet to prophet. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 18:15). And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 18:15): <b>כָּמֹנִי</b> (\"like me\") means that he will be a prophet of HaShem, not a soothsayer or diviner. And it is possible that <b>מִקִּרְבְּךָ</b> means that you will be able to trust his words, since he is from your brothers, from among you. And so in my opinion <b>כָּמֹנִי</b> means that he will be faithful as a prophet of HaShem, and you shall believe in him just as you believe in me. And I will further explain this:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:51:32.587815864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}